   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "כֹּהֶנֶת מִטַּמְּאָה כּוּ׳. מַאי טַעְמָא — אָמַר קְרָא: ״אֱמֹר אֶל הַכֹּהֲנִים בְּנֵי אַהֲרֹן״. בְּנֵי אַהֲרֹן וְלֹא בְּנוֹת אַהֲרֹן.",
   "en": "The mishna states: «A daughter of a priest may become impure» with impurity imparted by a corpse, but a priest may not. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» for this? The Gemara answers: «The verse states: “Speak to the priests, the sons of Aaron,» and say to them: None shall become impure for the dead among his people” (Leviticus 21:1). The verse indicates that this applies to «the sons of Aaron and not» to «the daughters of Aaron.»"
  }
 ],
